You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Typing Placeholder Input (`input-typing-placeholder`)

A search field whose placeholder types out example queries, pauses and deletes them — and stops the moment you focus or type.

## What it should do
Build an input with an animated placeholder: while the field is empty and unfocused, an aria-hidden overlay types suggestions character by character (55 ms ± jitter), pauses, deletes at double speed and moves to the next. Hide the native placeholder visually (placeholder:text-transparent) but keep it for screen readers. Stop on focus or value.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **js**.
- No runtime dependencies (CSS only).
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/input-typing-placeholder.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** A real static placeholder is set for assistive tech; the animated text is aria-hidden and hidden on focus. Reduced motion: suggestions swap whole.
- **Performance:** setTimeout loop only while idle; stops on focus/value.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

